  "title": "Sun Quan Submits to Wei to Buy a Free Hand",
  "year": "221-222",
  "summary": [
    "Sun Quan, facing the whole of Shu with Wei at his back, accepts a Wei title and calls himself a subject — a humiliation he takes without visible difficulty, because it costs nothing and buys him one front instead of two.",
    "Liu Bei comes down the gorges taking city after city. For a season it looks as though grief is a workable strategy."
  ],
  "history": "Historical. Sun Quan's willingness to be seen to submit whenever it was useful is one of the more consistent things about him.",
